**Database Project – Team Roles & Work Distribution**

Hi everyone,

We are starting the execution of our Database Project (Phase 1 – Asset Management System).

We are 6 members, so I've divided the work into 6 responsibilities. Each member should choose their assigned role and start working on their deliverables.

**1. Team Roles & Responsibilities**

**Member 1 – Project Manager & Database Integration**

- Coordinate the team and follow up on progress.
- Create the database in Microsoft SQL Server.
- Configure the required database files (MDF, NDF and 2 LDF files).
- Collect and integrate all SQL scripts.
- Make sure everything works together.
- Prepare the final submission.

**Member 2 – ERD Designer**

- Create the Entity Relationship Diagram using draw\.io.
- Include all 7 entities, attributes, PKs and FKs.
- Show all relationships and cardinalities (1 and M).
- Export the digital diagram to PDF.
- Prepare the hand-drawn ERD version.

**Member 3 – Mapping Diagram Designer**

- Create the Mapping Diagram using draw\.io.
- Convert the approved ERD into relational tables.
- Include all columns, data types, PKs and FKs.
- Draw arrows connecting every FK to its referenced PK.
- Export the digital diagram to PDF.
- Prepare the hand-drawn Mapping Diagram.

**Member 4 – SQL Tables Developer**

- Write the CREATE TABLE scripts.
- Define all columns using the agreed data types.
- Implement all Primary Keys and Foreign Keys.
- Make sure the relationships match the approved diagrams.
- Deliver the SQL script ready for integration.

**Member 5 – SQL Constraints Developer**

- Implement UNIQUE constraints.
- Implement CHECK constraints.
- Implement DEFAULT constraints.
- Ensure all mandatory columns have NOT NULL.
- Use clear and consistent constraint names.
- Test that the constraints work correctly.

**Member 6 – Testing & Documentation**

- Prepare realistic sample data.
- Write INSERT scripts.
- Test the relationships and constraints.
- Test invalid data to ensure constraints reject it.
- Capture screenshots from SQL Server.
- Prepare the testing documentation.

